    },
    "message": "Move information_spread_v1 and the sample step of the information model to Rust\n\nRust owns the namespace in native/src/state/information.rs. The step\n_sample_information_contacts runs native/src/rules/information.rs, with claims and\nbeliefs, for the three information policies, and the namespace is no longer written\nwhole each tick: the tree gets single values, and the contact records are refilled.\nAgents come from the entity rows. A trace, another RNG, a policy's subclass and any\nstate the Python rule might raise on give Unsupported, and the Python step runs.\n\nThe kernel no longer needs InformationSpreadPolicy.native_update, and its validator\nreplaces the Python validation of the namespace when it accepts.\n\nbenchmarks/rule_shadow/information_shadow.py compares every draw, contact,\nprobability and event with the Python rule. rng.rs and world_core.rs take the same\ndraw log and refill_record_map as the social propagation lane, line for line.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
